{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1577593005,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2OTQ3MzA1MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3965#issuecomment-569473051"},"message":"\u003e datalad says \"add\" for existing subdataset during save -- bug ?\n\nI believe \"add\" is the intended action for saving modifications to an existing dataset.  It's an \"add\" in the `git add` sense: the new hash for updated subdataset (submodule) is being added to the index of the superdataset, in the same way that a modified or new regular file is added to the index.  (Ideally, though, I'd say the type of these records should be \"dataset\" rather than \"file\".)\n\nBased on ...\n\n\u003e Out of the 8 subdatasets above, 3 are newly added, 5 were already there but had been modified. However, when doing the save at this top level, it reports all 8 as being an \"add\".\n\n... I think the core issue you're raising is that you think adding a new submodule and adding modifications to a different one should have distinct actions (?).  Before 3dd23bf26 (BF: gitrepo: Yield 'add' result when saving new submodule, 2019-05-10), we actually didn't report anything when adding a new submodule, while staging a modified submodule reported a result record with an action of \"add\".  As [mentioned][0] in that PR, I was on the fence about whether adding a new submodule should have an action of \"add\" or something else (specifically \"add_submodule\").  \n\nIs your preference based on the need to act on distinct records for new vs modified subdatasets, or is it just that you find the current presentation confusing?\n\n[0]: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3398#discussion_r282928154","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"16b99348182e0cea45e7ee70866e8671634ada6a"},"timestamp":1577593364,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2OTQ3MzM4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3965#issuecomment-569473380"},"message":"Thanks for responding @kyleam . I didn't consider all nuances to this issue and appreciate the explanation. For me, it was primarily the fact that I found the current presentation confusing.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1578332182,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MTIzMzY0MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3965#issuecomment-571233641"},"message":"Okay, no one else has weighed in, and, despite agreeing that using an action of \"add\" for existing but modified subdatasets may confuse some users, I don't have any particular ideas on an action and/or rendering that'd be better. \n\nI'll close this given it's not actionable at this point, but please feel free to continue the discussion.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1578332183,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjkyNDk3NDk5MA=="},"status":2}]}